    "narrative": "A nationwide addressable market of 338 million device-dependent consumers positions FixHub to capture same-day repair demand concentrated in young, tech-saturated, working communities.\n\nAcross all 52 geographic areas covering 338,067,439 residents, the demographic landscape aligns strongly with FixHub's same-day repair model. Age emerges as the single most powerful predictor of device ownership and heavy daily usage — the exact behaviors that produce cracked screens, degraded batteries, and data-loss emergencies. Median ages range from as low as 22 to 30.6, and the youngest, most tech-saturated markets generate the highest volume of repair-generating device activity. These areas represent FixHub's peak-traffic opportunity, where smartphone, tablet, and laptop penetration is deepest and the tolerance for downtime is lowest.\n\nAffordability data reinforces the case for repair over replacement. With median household incomes spanning $31K to $75K across areas, a large share of customers face a clear economic trade-off: pay for an affordable screen or battery repair, or absorb the far higher cost of a new device. This income band is FixHub's sweet spot — households with genuine reliance on their devices but limited appetite for premium replacement spending. Education levels layer onto this, correlating with device sophistication and greater comfort engaging professional data-recovery services, which command higher margins.\n\nMarket stability indicators confirm long-term commercial viability. Labor-force participation ranges from 28% up to 98%, and areas at the higher end signal both disposable income and a work-related dependence on functioning devices that makes fast turnaround especially valuable. Rent levels between $973 and $2,185 map cost-of-living and the presence of settled, recurring customer bases around each kiosk. Together, these signals let FixHub distinguish transient markets from durable, repeat-business locations.",
